  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Seliwanoff test for ketose and Xenthoprotic test for proteins.</p><p>Seliwanoff&#39;s test is a chemical test which distinguishes between aldose and ketose sugars. If the sugar contains a ketone group, it is a ketose. If a sugar contains an aldehyde group, it is an aldose. This test relies on the principle that, when heated, ketoses are more rapidly dehydrated than aldoses.</p>",
